  {
   "k": "j6280v",
   "en": "Prior to 1932, ⟦0⟧ was ruled by an absolute monarch. However, in 1932, a coup d'etat by the Khana Ratsadon, or People's Party, forced the monarch to abide by a constitution and yield much of his power to a civilian government. The reigning monarch, Prajadhipok or formally Rama VII, was initially accepting of a constitutional government. A 1933 counter-coup of which he played a minor role in failed after Phraya Phahon, one of the Khana Ratsadon's leading military officers, regained control over government. An armed revolt led by Prince Boworadej attempted once again in late 1933 to restore Rama VII's power, but this too failed. Continual disagreements with the Khana Ratsadon-led government under Phraya Phahon resulted in Rama VII voluntarily abdicating and go into exile in the ⟦1⟧ in 1935, eventually dying there in 1941, still in exile. His son, Ananda Mahidol, who was with him in exile, was next in line for the Siamese throne.",
